course: dictionary
lesson: 7512
title: Pounce: a sudden jump
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pounce is a verb: it means to jump suddenly onto something to catch it. Read the clues around it. «Cats hunt by waiting, creeping and pouncing.» Waiting and creeping come first, so the pounce is the sudden final jump.
explain: Pounce can also be a noun, «a pounce», meaning a sudden jump. It can mean to quickly attack or criticise a mistake or a chance, as in «She pounced on the chance to go». Check by swapping in another word: «She jumped on the chance to go» still fits, so the meaning is grabbed quickly.
explain: Look out for phrases: «pounce on», «pounce upon», «ready to pounce» and «pounce on a mistake». In these, the word is about a quick, sudden action, not a slow one.
fact: Pounce means to jump suddenly onto something to catch it.
fact: Cats are ambush hunters, so they wait quietly and then pounce.
fact: Cats judge distance well and notice moving things more easily than still ones.
fact: As a noun, «a pounce» is a sudden jump to catch something.
fact: «Pounce on a mistake» means to quickly criticise it.
exercise: «Cats hunt by waiting, creeping and pouncing.» What does pouncing mean here? | Drinking milk quietly | *Jumping suddenly onto something to catch it | Running in a long, slow race | Sleeping in a warm spot
exercise: «She pounced on the chance to go.» What does pounced mean here? | Slowly thought about it | Wrote it down neatly | *Quickly grabbed | Forgot all about it
exercise: Which sentence uses pounce as a noun, meaning a sudden jump? | «The cat walked home along the wall.» | «The cat drank its milk slowly.» | *«The cat made a sudden pounce at the toy.» | «The cat was asleep on the warm mat.»
test: «He pounced on his friend's mistake in the spelling test.» What does pounced on mean here? | Forgot about it | Quietly forgave | *Quickly criticised | Copied it neatly
test: Which phrase means ready to attack suddenly? | *Ready to pounce | Ready to read | Ready for bed | Ready to sleep
exam: «Cats hunt by waiting, creeping and pouncing, not by long wild chases.» What does this tell you about how a cat hunts? | *It waits quietly and then makes a sudden jump | It runs very fast for a long time | It swims to catch fish | It sleeps all day
